  "mandatoryInvariants": [
    "only canonical server snapshots can authorize moderation transitions",
    "every command uses a stable UUID clientRequestId and optimistic revisions",
    "same command identity and fingerprint replays the same outcome",
    "payload drift under the same idempotency key is a conflict",
    "reports open a case but do not automatically hide, remove or alter reputation",
    "triage does not alter public visibility",
    "hide and remove require an authoritative under-review case",
    "dismissal closes the case without manufacturing a new review",
    "appeals can be submitted only by the review author",
    "appeals do not automatically restore public visibility",
    "appeal decisions require an independent senior moderator",
    "restore and deny-appeal commands bind to the exact prior decision event",
    "moderators cannot decide cases involving themselves as author, reviewed user or reporter",
    "event envelopes are append-only and hash chained",
    "raw evidence, credentials, payment data and private message bodies are prohibited",
    "public visibility is derived from review state and never selected by the browser",
    "moderation acceptance alone grants no reputation mutation authority",
    "localStorage, cache and local mock state never establish moderation authority"
  ],
